<title>USA: Mich. Senate okays using rainy day fund for roads.</title>
<headline>Mich. Senate okays using rainy day fund for roads.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Michigan Senate on Thursday approved a bill that would siphon about $69 million in interest from the state's burgeoning rainy day fund to pay for road projects.</p>
<p>The 33 to 3 vote sent the bill onto the House for consideration, according to the Senate Republican majority communications office.</p>
<p>The bill would limit the use of interest earnings from the state's $1.1 billion rainy day fund to fiscal 1998, which begins Oct. 1. A spokesman for Gov. John Engler was not available to comment on the governor's position on the bill.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
